"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NDc3NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3447762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny","html_url":"https://github.com/samjanny","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samjanny/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-22T17:00:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-22T17:00:05Z","body":"> Is there an issue created for this?\r\n\r\nI haven't found an existing issue that isolates this exact dilation bug yet. #112768 may be related because it reports lightmap shifting/misalignment and notes a change in behavior around 4.4, but I haven't verified that it is caused by the same dilation logic.\r\n\r\nIn this case the regression is very specific: since 054340bb6, the dilation pass also searches neighboring texels when the current texel is already valid, so a valid texel can be replaced by the first valid neighbor found. In the instrumented repro, 57/57 valid texels were overwritten before the fix, while after the fix all 57 kept their original RGBA and the 2 empty texels were still filled correctly.\r\n\r\nSo I would consider #112768 potentially related, but not confirmed to be the same issue. I haven't found a report yet that isolates the valid-texel overwrite specifically.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5780594257/reactions